    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3545f577_c0f560b7",
        "filename": "packages/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T12:56:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we don\u0027t need to spell out \"IN_NETWORK_CAPABILITIES\". Sure, today it\u0027s the only place, but if we have more in the future say in LinkProperties I think it\u0027s extremely likely that we\u0027ll want to use the same flag. If not, then we\u0027ll deprecate this name and add a new name for NC only.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3279,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 3279,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "bc31695b96c023d8bb9656df38887d0e1518247e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10caa9c0_f80d85fb",
        "filename": "packages/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T23:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, makes sense. I didn\u0027t do that because we already have a bunch of location sensitive data in LinkProperties which we instead made it available only for settings app a few years back. Reference: https://source.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java;rcl\u003da888b76e44ad229a8a728c4f403836cb08aa992c;l\u003d1870\n\n\nMy concern with removing the \"IN_NETWORK_CAPABILITIES\" is what happens to those existing location sensitive fields in LinkProperties.\nOptions: \n1. Do nothing. We continue to only make the existing fields available to apps with `NETWORK_SETTINGS`. Any new fields in LinkProperties will be guarded with this flag.\n2. Change all existing fields to also be guarded by this flag (similar to ownerUid with a targetSdk check). But, this would be going back on a previous deprecation. Do we want to do that?",
      "parentUuid": "3545f577_c0f560b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3279,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 3279,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "bc31695b96c023d8bb9656df38887d0e1518247e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6386ed0_f956f1ff",
        "filename": "packages/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T17:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both of these options seem reasonable to me. We can also do #1 now and #2 in the future.\n\nWhat are the sensitive fields?",
      "parentUuid": "10caa9c0_f80d85fb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3279,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 3279,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "bc31695b96c023d8bb9656df38887d0e1518247e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "777eaf95_77dd4ba2",
        "filename": "packages/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T21:13:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 2 fields are:\n- mCaptivePortalData\n- mCaptivePortalApiUrl\n\nI might be wrong in my initial assessment. This is probably location sensitive (from the url, you can figure out location), but this might also be just privileged data. Do we want apps other than settings to get this info? If no, then nothing needs to change.",
      "parentUuid": "b6386ed0_f956f1ff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3279,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 3279,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "bc31695b96c023d8bb9656df38887d0e1518247e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "764e5a58_bfadba97",
        "filename": "packages/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1046,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T12:56:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s a bit more complex than this.\n\n  - The querying app has system permissions, or is the owner app itself\n  AND\n    - The app is the active VPN APP\n    OR\n      - The app has location permission\n      AND\n        - The app\u0027s target SDK is lower than S\n        OR\n        - The flag is included\n\nSo how to express this is a bit difficult, but at least we should say apps never get to see UIDs that are not their own. Suggested wording (feel free to improve, amend...) :\n\n  This field will only be populated for VPN and network suggestor apps,\n  and only for the network they own.\n  In the case of network suggestors, this field is also location sensitive,\n  so the app needs to hold LOCATION_FINE, and use FLAG_INCLUDE_LOCATION_INFO\n  in the request if they want to see it. They will then be blamed for\n  location access.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1042,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 1046,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "bc31695b96c023d8bb9656df38887d0e1518247e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
